  ],
  "text": "Chilli does not burn you. There is no heat involved anywhere. Your tongue carries a receptor whose only job is to report dangerous temperature. Capsaicin fits that receptor and switches it on directly. So your brain receives a genuine burning alarm with nothing actually burning. The pain is real. The heat is a lie. Menthol pulls the exact same trick in reverse, on the cold receptor. Birds do not have that receptor in a form capsaicin can jam, so they feel nothing. Which is the whole point. The plant wants birds to spread its seeds and mammals to leave it alone. And water does not help, because capsaicin is not water soluble. It only spreads it around. Milk works. The fat dissolves it and the protein drags it away. One of these every day. Follow so you do not miss tomorrow.",
  "voice": "802e3bc2b27e49c2995d23ef70e6ac89",
  "model": "s2.1-pro-free"
}
